1
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:04,720
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,230 --> 00:00:10,500
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,370 --> 00:00:14,390
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,470 --> 00:00:17,200
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:21,410
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:29,150 --> 00:00:33,250
Why does Griffith value you so much?

7
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:38,560
There's no reason...

8
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:39,600
...in particular.

9
00:00:41,330 --> 00:00:43,660
Do you really need a reason...

10
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:49,230
...each time I decide to lay
my life on the line for you?

11
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:12,510
Feel no shame about shape

12
00:01:12,590 --> 00:01:14,420
Weather changes their phrase

13
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:18,180
Even mother will show you another way

14
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:20,550
So put your glasses on

15
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:22,640
Nothing will be wrong

16
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:24,850
There's no blame. There's no fame

17
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:26,690
It's up to you

18
00:01:26,850 --> 00:01:30,310
The first words should be found

19
00:01:30,940 --> 00:01:33,940
Whatever holds you back

20
00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:35,320
I...

21
00:01:35,690 --> 00:01:36,450
...can...

22
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:38,610
I can get it off

23
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:39,620
Tell me what...

24
00:01:39,620 --> 00:01:40,620
Tell me what...

25
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:42,450
Tell me what you want

26
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:43,540
I don't know why...

27
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:44,540
Don't know why...

28
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:46,540
Don't know why you're afraid

29
00:01:46,710 --> 00:01:47,710
Tell me what...

30
00:01:47,790 --> 00:01:48,670
Tell me what...

31
00:01:48,830 --> 00:01:50,330
Tell me what you'd say

32
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:51,670
I don't know why...

33
00:01:51,790 --> 00:01:52,750
Don't know why...

34
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:53,550
Too late...

35
00:01:53,630 --> 00:01:55,170
It's too late

36
00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:04,100
Conspiracy

37
00:03:39,490 --> 00:03:40,440
All right!

38
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:42,150
Stretch out the rest of the ropes!

39
00:03:48,540 --> 00:03:50,450
Any sign of the enemy?

40
00:03:50,450 --> 00:03:52,000
Nothing at all.

41
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:58,380
Even if hundreds or thousands
of the enemy attempt an attack...

42
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:04,050
The elite of the valiant Blue Whale
Heavy Assault Knights are here.

43
00:04:04,050 --> 00:04:08,220
No one can set one foot in
a stronghold under our guard!

44
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,690
Listen...

45
00:04:15,690 --> 00:04:17,770
You must always be on your guard in war.

46
00:04:17,770 --> 00:04:19,610
Do not cease to be vigilant!

47
00:04:19,940 --> 00:04:20,480
Yes, sir!

48
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:35,210
Our commander is unusually alert.

49
00:04:35,210 --> 00:04:37,960
Yeah, it's because he's been
given such an important job.

50
00:04:38,460 --> 00:04:40,420
I suppose he cannot help but be enthusiastic.

51
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,690
Is it from Guts?

52
00:05:06,110 --> 00:05:08,620
No doubt.
It's the signal for the next phase!

53
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:10,370
Good!

54
00:05:10,370 --> 00:05:11,120
Let's move.

55
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,700
Enemy raid!

56
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,240
What?

57
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,620
An enemy raid?

58
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:50,570
Enemy raid!

59
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:52,080
Let's go!

60
00:05:51,910 --> 00:05:52,700
Ready!

61
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:55,250
Enemy raid!

62
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:35,660
They finally showed their faces!

63
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:36,250
Aye, sir!

64
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:40,960
Well, fire the cannons into
the center of their formation!

65
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:43,790
Sir, it is impossible
to reach them at this distance.

66
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:48,340
Then send out the whole unit
and tear those rotten kids apart!

67
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:48,970
Yes, sir!

68
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:51,140
Hold on a minute!

69
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:57,680
This is their trap!

70
00:06:58,850 --> 00:07:03,310
They must realize how difficult
it would be to destroy this stronghold.

71
00:07:03,310 --> 00:07:05,610
So they are plotting
to lead us out into the field!

72
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:08,610
How foolish they are!

73
00:07:08,610 --> 00:07:11,360
Such cheap tricks
are of no use against Sir Adon...

74
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:13,990
...the most resourceful
commander in the Tudor army.

75
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:16,240
Now what are we supposed to do?

76
00:07:18,450 --> 00:07:19,960
Ignore them.

77
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:21,170
What?

78
00:07:21,170 --> 00:07:23,420
Let them buzz around as they like!

79
00:07:44,190 --> 00:07:45,060
All right!

80
00:07:45,060 --> 00:07:46,480
It's time to get moving!

81
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,530
Griffith!

82
00:07:58,370 --> 00:08:02,040
I've confirmed that all
the Raiders have crossed the river!

83
00:08:02,410 --> 00:08:03,370
Excellent!

84
00:08:03,370 --> 00:08:05,790
Let us vanish from the sight of the enemy!

85
00:08:19,930 --> 00:08:22,430
It looks like they're pulling back!

86
00:08:22,770 --> 00:08:27,310
It's not worth risking their lives
to attack this impregnable stronghold!

87
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:08,020
Message!

88
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:08,810
Open the gate!

89
00:09:09,230 --> 00:09:10,110
What's happened?

90
00:09:10,610 --> 00:09:14,530
The general will be visiting this castle
regarding an important operation!

91
00:09:14,530 --> 00:09:16,110
R-Really?

92
00:09:16,110 --> 00:09:17,820
I'll pass the information
to your commander directly!

93
00:09:17,990 --> 00:09:18,820
Certainly!

94
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:39,010
W-What's this?

95
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:53,030
W-What's the meaning of this?

96
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:57,530
They snuck in from the rear gate!

97
00:09:58,740 --> 00:10:01,070
They disappeared and
then burst in from the back!

98
00:10:01,070 --> 00:10:02,700
What a dirty trick!

99
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,830
Blow them all apart!

100
00:10:04,830 --> 00:10:05,700
Y-Yes, sir!

101
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:07,500
We'll repel them with our entire force!

102
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:13,500
Should we send the signal now?

103
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:15,880
No, first we secure their way in!

104
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:17,510
It's an enemy raid!

105
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:20,590
Bring all the bridge
guards back into the castle!

106
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:36,610
Griffith...

107
00:10:36,610 --> 00:10:38,570
We shall wait for the signal.

108
00:10:38,570 --> 00:10:41,570
Can't he be quick about it?

109
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:45,290
I wonder why he puts so much faith in Guts...

110
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:46,750
What's going on?

111
00:10:46,750 --> 00:10:48,040
Why did you open the gate?

112
00:10:58,340 --> 00:10:59,260
Now!

113
00:10:59,260 --> 00:10:59,800
Yes, sir!

114
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:03,010
W-What was that?

115
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:05,720
Griffith!

116
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:08,310
Rush the front gate of the castle, quickly!

117
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:45,970
Shit!

118
00:11:45,970 --> 00:11:49,140
Do they think they can
succeed with such a small number?

119
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:55,440
I, Sir Adon, shall put
an end to their lives personally!

120
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:04,160
The enemy is breaking through the front!

121
00:12:08,290 --> 00:12:09,370
Damn it!

122
00:12:09,370 --> 00:12:12,710
What sneaky tactics,
charging in from both sides like that!

123
00:12:50,870 --> 00:12:53,750
We're caught between
the two groups. It's out of our control!

124
00:12:56,210 --> 00:12:58,590
Give us your next command, sir!

125
00:13:02,710 --> 00:13:03,590
Retreat!

126
00:13:04,130 --> 00:13:05,130
But...

127
00:13:05,130 --> 00:13:07,970
My brain is key to the Tudor Empire!

128
00:13:07,970 --> 00:13:10,220
I must avoid dying in vain here!

129
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:20,230
That's our commander!

130
00:13:20,230 --> 00:13:21,980
You had a raft prepared just in case!

131
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:23,610
I am always prepared!

132
00:13:24,150 --> 00:13:26,990
It is a commander's duty!

133
00:13:26,990 --> 00:13:28,110
C-Commander!

134
00:13:28,110 --> 00:13:28,700
Commander!

135
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:31,660
Please, take us with you.

136
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:32,870
Please!

137
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:37,250
Get away!

138
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:39,670
How outrageous of you!

139
00:13:39,670 --> 00:13:41,500
This raft is a precious heirloom...

140
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:43,840
...that has been handed down
through the Coborlwitz family!

141
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:45,970
Remove your armor!
You can all swim!

142
00:14:08,610 --> 00:14:09,950
You did well.

143
00:14:10,620 --> 00:14:12,530
I just followed your orders.

144
00:14:33,510 --> 00:14:34,810
We did it!

145
00:14:34,810 --> 00:14:38,100
Finally, we drove
a wedge into Tudor territory.

146
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:41,610
We've opened the pass leading to Doldrey.

147
00:14:57,910 --> 00:15:00,670
Oh boy, that was a long walk!

148
00:15:00,830 --> 00:15:03,250
First I'll feed my stomach
with a sumptuous meal...

149
00:15:03,250 --> 00:15:05,090
...and then I'll have a well-deserved rest!

150
00:15:14,260 --> 00:15:17,220
Y-Your Grace, General Boscone!

151
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:19,480
What happened to Fort Brax?

152
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:23,310
W-Well, our enemy
was so devious that...

153
00:15:23,310 --> 00:15:27,940
...even I was inferior in terms
of underhanded trickery, sir.

154
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:31,110
So did you just roll over
and surrender the fortress?

155
00:15:31,610 --> 00:15:34,950
No, I deliberately withdrew and
let them occupy the fort temporarily...

156
00:15:34,950 --> 00:15:37,620
...to give us ample time to regroup, sir...

157
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:38,540
Enough lies!

158
00:15:39,620 --> 00:15:43,250
Do you comprehend how important
that fort was to deployment?

159
00:15:43,250 --> 00:15:45,090
W-Well, sir...

160
00:15:45,090 --> 00:15:48,590
I'm warning you. This is
the last time I will support you!

161
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:51,260
Lord Boscone...

162
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:54,050
A warrior must always follow
the principles of honor and justice!

163
00:15:54,050 --> 00:15:55,680
This is true now and always!

164
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:56,550
Yes, sir!

165
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:12,320
This time, I shall put an end
to them with the secret tactics...

166
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:15,570
...that have been passed down
the Coborlwitz family for 500 years!

167
00:16:15,570 --> 00:16:17,740
No doubt about it!

168
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:19,620
It's 500 years now?

169
00:16:24,330 --> 00:16:27,540
Not quarreling with some evil design...

170
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:29,590
Not straying from virtue...

171
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:32,170
Sacrifice thyself ceaselessly...

172
00:16:32,170 --> 00:16:36,140
Render your services to
our fief for peace and security...

173
00:16:36,140 --> 00:16:39,600
The title of count is
bestowed upon thee...

174
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:42,980
Place thy flesh and heart in heaven.

175
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:46,900
Separate thyself from falsehood...

176
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:51,190
Uphold the law, know the subjects...

177
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:58,740
Be valiant, and with due
majesty, advance the war.

178
00:16:58,740 --> 00:17:05,580
Stand prepared for thy foe with
due thirst for battle and fear not.

179
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:10,960
Despite the machinations of
thy foes who march upon thee...

180
00:17:11,630 --> 00:17:17,260
...the duly appointed count
of our glorious kingdom of Midland...

181
00:17:24,140 --> 00:17:26,140
He has become a count...

182
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:28,060
Say, did you hear about it?

183
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:30,900
Sir Griffith was awarded the title of count!

184
00:17:31,230 --> 00:17:32,440
I've heard that too!

185
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:34,570
He's so handsome!

186
00:17:34,570 --> 00:17:39,280
I'm jealous because he's so attractive
and more graceful than any woman!

187
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:40,200
Not only that...

188
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:42,330
...he is the greatest swordsman in the kingdom...

189
00:17:42,330 --> 00:17:44,120
...and commands the strongest army!

190
00:17:44,410 --> 00:17:46,710
He is far more classy
than those awkward nobles...

191
00:17:46,710 --> 00:17:49,830
...and he has so much
presence and elegance!

192
00:17:49,830 --> 00:17:56,550
True, compared to him, those
court ministers are all rude and rough.

193
00:17:57,010 --> 00:18:00,930
The poor officials just
can't compare to Sir Griffith!

194
00:18:01,510 --> 00:18:02,470
You women!

195
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:05,520
You should not speak of such things!

196
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:07,480
W-We are sorry, Your Excellency!

197
00:18:09,480 --> 00:18:11,060
Those gossipers...

198
00:18:11,610 --> 00:18:13,400
General Julius...

199
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:19,780
What use is yelling if your
voice echoes throughout the court?

200
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:29,040
You look very
displeased for some reason.

201
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:31,790
It makes me wonder what is wrong.

202
00:18:31,790 --> 00:18:32,960
It is no concern of yours!

203
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:36,970
Oh, yes.

204
00:18:36,970 --> 00:18:41,390
Did Your Grace
happen to learn about...

205
00:18:41,390 --> 00:18:45,100
...the king's escort
for the upcoming fall hunt?

206
00:18:45,850 --> 00:18:47,060
In that matter...

207
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:51,650
...my unit, the White Dragon Knights,
are regularly assigned to the task.

208
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:53,480
What is your point?

209
00:18:53,650 --> 00:19:00,160
The Band of the Hawk was requested
as escort by imperial decree.

210
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,610
T-That cannot be!

211
00:19:01,950 --> 00:19:03,830
It is reliable information...

212
00:19:04,370 --> 00:19:05,450
Nonsense!

213
00:19:05,450 --> 00:19:07,830
The fall hunt is an important
event that allows the king...

214
00:19:07,830 --> 00:19:09,960
...to promote friendly relations
between feudal lords.

215
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:13,290
Our best knights, the White
Dragons, are the only ones...

216
00:19:13,290 --> 00:19:16,710
...who are allowed to serve
the king in that honorable assignment.

217
00:19:16,710 --> 00:19:20,300
How could those upstart
thieves take that from us?

218
00:19:22,390 --> 00:19:25,680
What is His Majesty thinking?

219
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:28,350
Will you allow this affair to take place?

220
00:19:28,350 --> 00:19:29,270
What do you mean?

221
00:19:29,270 --> 00:19:33,730
The White Dragons were reputed
to be the strongest unit in the kingdom.

222
00:19:33,730 --> 00:19:36,690
Nevertheless, their glory
has turned insignificant...

223
00:19:36,690 --> 00:19:38,940
...due to the Band of the Hawk's rise.

224
00:19:38,940 --> 00:19:41,280
Y-You...

225
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:42,660
This is a rumor.

226
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:45,070
As I say, it is a rumor within the court.

227
00:19:47,040 --> 00:19:52,420
It is an unmistakable fact that
the Band of the Hawk is invincible.

228
00:19:52,830 --> 00:19:56,960
There is no sign that the
disturbances of war will subside soon.

229
00:19:57,380 --> 00:20:02,340
Therefore, that man will keep winning
honors through his military exploits.

230
00:20:02,970 --> 00:20:07,850
Additionally, His Majesty highly
values that boy, as you can see.

231
00:20:07,850 --> 00:20:10,850
So while I don't know how
he won His Majesty's favor...

232
00:20:10,850 --> 00:20:15,020
If things go badly, that boy
might become a general...

233
00:20:15,020 --> 00:20:16,060
Do not talk nonsense!

234
00:20:16,060 --> 00:20:17,730
I would never permit it!

235
00:20:17,730 --> 00:20:20,320
It is unheard of, some upstart
mercenary becoming a general!

236
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:24,700
That bastard could be a general like I am?

237
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:31,870
That man of common origins
would be on the same level as me?

238
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:36,130
Well, I just mentioned the
possibility. That which could be...

239
00:20:36,130 --> 00:20:37,090
I won't allow it!

240
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,130
I absolutely will not allow it!

241
00:20:43,130 --> 00:20:46,390
However, some danger always
lies in the act of hunting...

242
00:20:46,390 --> 00:20:48,550
...despite the fact it is an imperial event.

243
00:20:50,470 --> 00:20:56,150
You never know what kind of
beasts hide within the woods...

244
00:20:56,730 --> 00:20:58,230
What are you trying to say?

245
00:20:58,230 --> 00:21:00,480
Of course, not only are the beasts dangerous...

246
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:04,610
...but so are the stray arrows that may
have been launched at the beasts.

247
00:21:05,070 --> 00:21:06,160
A stray arrow?

248
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:12,370
And a nastily-poisoned stray arrow at that...

249
00:21:14,210 --> 00:21:16,370
If you mean...

250
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:19,460
A stray arrow, General.

251
00:21:29,430 --> 00:21:31,060
A stray arrow...

252
00:21:31,060 --> 00:21:32,220
Interesting!

253
00:21:33,390 --> 00:21:36,850
It would be a proper death
for a man of common birth!

254
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

255
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

256
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

257
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

258
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

259
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

260
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

261
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

262
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

263
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

264
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

